  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4102.29 Bug and tar remover",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4102.29 “Bug and tar remover” means a product designed to remove either or both of the following from painted motor vehicle surfaces without causing damage to the finish:\n\n(a) Biological-type residues, such as insect carcasses and tree sap; or\n\n(b) Road grime, such as road tar, roadway paint markings, and asphalt.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
}
